{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01798",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.61,
      "end_seconds": 3.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Good afternoon, how are you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.25,
      "end_seconds": 5.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "Evening, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.74,
      "end_seconds": 8.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Alright, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.13,
      "end_seconds": 15.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "I wanted to get swollen glands in my neck looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.33,
      "end_seconds": 25.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.35,
      "end_seconds": 33.55,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "It's been like this since Friday. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.4,
      "end_seconds": 37.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.44,
      "end_seconds": 51.04,
      "duration_seconds": 11.6,
      "text": "I'd say mild. As for feeling exhausted, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.66,
      "end_seconds": 54.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.13,
      "end_seconds": 64.93,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "I'd call it mild. And a fever, too. With fever, I'd say mild. I'd say all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.04,
      "end_seconds": 69.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.73,
      "end_seconds": 73.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "My mother had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.47,
      "end_seconds": 80.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.11,
      "end_seconds": 86.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "I don't think I have any, uh, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.85,
      "end_seconds": 105.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.31,
      "end_seconds": 124.26,
      "duration_seconds": 16.95,
      "text": "I'm on rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night. Though honestly, some days I forget to take it. Metoprolol. I take it 50 milligrams, twice a day for my pressure. Throat lozenges. I take it when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.6,
      "end_seconds": 128.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Ah. Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.11,
      "end_seconds": 138.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "High cholesterol, for about a year. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.23,
      "end_seconds": 139.93,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Ah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.21,
      "end_seconds": 145.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.49,
      "end_seconds": 155.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.62,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure is known to us, good to have that clear. Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.77,
      "end_seconds": 161.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.89,
      "end_seconds": 164.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.31,
      "end_seconds": 170.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.17,
      "end_seconds": 174.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Okay, anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.2,
      "end_seconds": 180.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.26,
      "end_seconds": 191.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.16,
      "end_seconds": 197.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "I had part of my thyroid removed years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.86,
      "end_seconds": 201.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "A few quick ones: jaundice, rash or difficulty breathing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.54,
      "end_seconds": 207.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "No, no jaundice, rash or difficulty breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.12,
      "end_seconds": 212.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Has there been any tummy pain on the left?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.31,
      "end_seconds": 217.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Definitely no tummy pain on the left."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.17,
      "end_seconds": 221.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.39,
      "end_seconds": 224.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.35,
      "end_seconds": 229.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.38,
      "end_seconds": 246.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.75,
      "end_seconds": 264.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "Okay: heart rate 90, saturation 95 percent, temperature 38.2, pressure 120 over 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.45,
      "end_seconds": 267.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.35,
      "end_seconds": 273.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.43,
      "end_seconds": 278.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.58,
      "end_seconds": 282.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.06,
      "end_seconds": 304.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "Your tonsils are large with white coating and the glands in the neck are tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.73,
      "end_seconds": 309.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.11,
      "end_seconds": 335.31,
      "duration_seconds": 15.2,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, this looks most like glandular fever. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I can't rule out streptococcal tonsillitis yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.23,
      "end_seconds": 340.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Well, I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.45,
      "end_seconds": 360.74,
      "duration_seconds": 19.29,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now glandular fever is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had swollen glands in your neck, since Friday, mild, and no rash or jaundice."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.45,
      "end_seconds": 364.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Mm, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.18,
      "end_seconds": 384.09,
      "duration_seconds": 17.91,
      "text": "I'm going to order a monospot test, for sore throat and fatigue. Rest, plenty of fluids, and no contact sport for a month because of the spleen. Please come and see me in two weeks. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.69,
      "end_seconds": 387.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.49,
      "end_seconds": 389.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}